reference=[('Two SDK responses, six UI actions', 'The callback ultimately returns allow or deny. Editing and remembering enrich allow; suggestions enrich deny. Redirect is a separate streaming user message, not a third PermissionResult behavior.'), ('Actual suggestions and session scope', 'The app records the SDK suggestions and selects only acceptEdits or allow/addRules proposals for Write. Their destination is deliberately changed to session. This teaches remembered permissions without writing persistent settings. No suggestion is fabricated when the SDK supplies none.'), ('Suppressed remember control', 'If suppressAlwaysAllowRule is true, or no eligible Write suggestion exists, the UI disables remember and the server refuses it. The seven offline tests verify the unsupported-choice and suppression paths.'), ('Cancellation needs settlement', 'The slide removes an aborted request from its map. This implementation also resolves the pending promise as cancellation, clears its timer and removes its listener. Timeout and disconnected-browser aborts never grant approval.'), ('Local teaching scope', 'This loopback teaching server has one active run and same-origin POST checks. Random request IDs are single-use capabilities. A deployed multi-user product must bind requests to authenticated owners and provide its own authorization and durable lifecycle.'), ('A callback is not a universal hook', 'Read is pre-approved for the suggestion/redirect task. The pre-approved Write comparison demonstrates a real zero-callback run. A separate PreToolUse guard bounds all allowed paths and content sizes.'), ('Terminal create/delete exercise', 'The terminal app exposes only the disposable Write and the exact Bash command rm -- result.txt. A bounded PreToolUse ask decision routes both to y/n review. Answer y for creation and n for deletion. Host cleanup later removes only the verified temporary run directory.'), ('API usage and truthful evidence', 'The browser sends actual decisions to actual SDK calls. Nine experiments include a second model turn for redirect. The $0.40 SDK budget threshold is not a prepaid cap. Media, dependencies and credentials stay outside Git.')]
document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Every architecture step has source-linked coloured code.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 30 · Approvals in your UI\n\nFive linked student pages, large text, actual SDK experiments and coloured code in all thirteen UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson30-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson30-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson30-ui-approvals`. Open http://127.0.0.1:3130 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit and model access are required. Windows may require Git Bash.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file. Enter your own model key, then restart. Existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo GitHub token or Managed Agents IDs are required. Secrets, dependencies and teaching media stay outside Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, selected lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Official SDK approvals documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/user-input)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. Run `npm test` for offline boundaries, review lifecycle, workspace and startup checks.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 30 pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
